From ef571046b081962329f1ccb89b65ae22fc989130 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:20:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 06/51] kv-store: one node per process, warmup on registered
 workers, value checks

- node_id from config; NUMA strict policy and getcpu checks removed.
- Warmup Puts run on the worker threads themselves (registrations per
  node are never freed: workers + wmeta manager <= 32, checked).
  Every node warms the whole key space.
- Put writes a self-describing value (key, stamp, derived words); Get
  checks key and contents and counts misses/short reads/bad values. The
  run exits 3 if any check fails. write_ratio 0 keeps upstream's
  data-less read-only warmup and checks misses only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
